  c) modify your local copy for your own private use, for example to learn or to fix
     something for yourself, as long as the modified copy is not shared with anyone else;
  d) use the Engine, the hosted Realot Studio editor and the bundled templates to make
     Your Game.

3. YOUR GAMES BELONG TO YOU

You own Your Game. You may publish it, host it online, sell it, license it and make money
from it in any way You like, with no fee and no royalty to the Licensor.

You may distribute an Exported Game together with the Engine runtime files that the export
feature puts into it. This permission covers the game only. It does not allow You to
distribute the editor, the hub or the rest of the Engine, and an Exported Game must not be
used as a way to hand out or sell the Engine itself.

Owning Your Game does not give You ownership of the Engine. Material that comes with the
Engine (templates, sample art, sounds and scripts) is licensed to You only for use inside
Your Game, and You may not repackage it as a stand-alone product, asset pack or template.

